 "prompt": "Forecast the price of copper (USD per tonne, LME cash settlement) as of December 31, 2027. Establish the baseline: current LME price as of late October 2026, 2024-2026 trajectory, and current inventories. Research and weigh the principal drivers: Mine supply disruptions and grades (Chile, Peru, Panama/Cobre restart odds); new project pipelines (Kamoa-Kakula, El Tejon etc.); smelting capacity and TC/RC collapse; demand from grids, EVs, datacenters and construction (China property vs electrification); substitution and scrap; COMEX/LME spread and US tariff policy on metals. Deliverables: 3-5 mutually exclusive scenarios with probabilities, a most-likely trajectory, and at least 10 binary forecasts with concrete thresholds, counts or dates, each with a probability and resolution criteria anchored to verifiable sources.",
